<!-- SECTION 1 -->
<h2>1. Executive Summary &amp; Project Charter</h2>
<p>
  <strong>Disha Pariwar Charitable Trust</strong>, established in 2007 with headquarters at Narayan Peth, Laxmi Road, Pune, provides higher-education scholarships to underprivileged and meritorious students across rural Maharashtra (spanning Vidarbha, Marathwada, Khandesh, and Western Maharashtra). Historically, the scholarship application workflow relied on physical paper forms, manual postal correspondence, and localized paper filing, resulting in lengthy verification cycles, lost document submissions, and zero tracking transparency for remote applicants.
</p>
<p>
  This 3-to-4 month engineering project (August through November 2026) executed a complete digital transformation to design, develop, test, and deploy <strong>Release 2.0 of the Disha Pariwar Portal</strong>. The portal provides an inclusive, mobile-first, 100% bilingual (Marathi / English) digital application ecosystem with real-time status tracking, administrative evaluation dashboards, and offline PDF verification fallbacks.
</p>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Key Objectives Achieved:</strong>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zero Barrier Access:</strong> Built a lightweight, high-performance React 19 Single Page Application operating reliably on 2G/3G rural networks with sub-1.2s First Contentful Paint.</li>
    <li><strong>Bilingual Parity:</strong> Seamless client-side language switching between Marathi (मराठी) and English without page refreshes.</li>
    <li><strong>End-to-End Application Tracking:</strong> Instant inquiry by Reference Number (e.g. <code>DP-2026-XXXX</code>) or registered phone number with step-by-step progress visualizer.</li>
    <li><strong>Trustee Review Portal:</strong> Role-based review dashboard allowing administrators to filter applications, view applicant dossiers, and update statuses (Pending, In Review, Approved, Disbursed, Rejected).</li>
    <li><strong>Clean Codebase Governance:</strong> Removed 100% of legacy static HTML files and duplicate assets, achieving a pristine v2.0 architecture ready for long-term scalability.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

