    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Sprint 3</strong><br>(Sep 1 – Sep 14)</td>
      <td>
        <ul>
          <li>Implemented responsive layout shell with global Header, Language Switcher, and Footer.</li>
          <li>Built informational pages: Home (Vision, Impact metrics, Founder details), About Us, Eligibility Criteria, How to Apply, and Contact.</li>
          <li>Engineered accessible FAQ accordion with clear visual indicator affordances (+/- states).</li>
          <li>Configured client-side bilingual state provider (LanguageContext).</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td>
        <ul>
          <li>Daily standup velocity tracking.</li>
          <li>Weekly stakeholder demo of public portal pages.</li>
          <li>Mobile responsive audit across iOS and Android viewports.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-success">M2.1: Public Portal Alpha</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Sprint 4</strong><br>(Sep 15 – Sep 30)</td>
      <td>
        <ul>
          <li>Engineered 3-Step Scholarship Application Engine (<code>/apply</code>):
            <ol>
              <li>Personal &amp; Contact Details</li>
              <li>Academic History &amp; College Enrollment</li>
              <li>Family Income, Bank Details &amp; Document Checklist</li>
            </ol>
          </li>
          <li>Built live client-side validation for Aadhaar (12 digits), Mobile (10 digits), and Percentage ranges.</li>
          <li>Implemented unique Reference Number generator (e.g. <code>DP-2026-XXXX</code>).</li>
          <li>Developed Application Tracking Engine (<code>/dashboard</code>) with progress stepper.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td>
        <ul>
          <li>Mid-term Project Review with Trust Secretary.</li>
          <li>Code review and static code analysis.</li>
          <li>Burn-down chart verification (100% on schedule).</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-success">M2.2: Application System Alpha</span></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

