<!-- SECTION 5 -->
<h2>5. Risk Management Matrix &amp; Mitigation Strategies</h2>
<p>
  Throughout the project lifecycle, the Project Manager maintained a proactive Risk Register. The top risks and executed mitigation actions are outlined below:
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 20%;">Identified Risk</th>
      <th style="width: 15%;">Severity / Probability</th>
      <th style="width: 35%;">Impact Description</th>
      <th style="width: 30%;">Mitigation Action Executed</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Poor Internet Connectivity in Rural Tehsils</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-danger">High</span> / <span class="badge badge-danger">High</span></td>
      <td>Students in remote villages unable to submit heavy web forms or upload documents.</td>
      <td>Optimized payload to &lt;200KB initial bundle; built offline printable PDF form download allowing postal/manual submission as a backup channel.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Marathi Font Inconsistency across Devices</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-warning">Medium</span> / <span class="badge badge-danger">High</span></td>
      <td>Devanagari conjunct consonants breaking on older budget Android phones.</td>
      <td>Implemented robust native Devanagari system font fallbacks (Nirmala UI, Noto Sans Devanagari) with Unicode UTF-8 strict compliance.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Incomplete or Fraudulent Income Submissions</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-danger">High</span> / <span class="badge badge-warning">Medium</span></td>
      <td>Applications submitted without valid Tehsildar income certificates.</td>
      <td>Enforced mandatory checklist verification in Step 3; built evaluator flag system in the Admin Portal for physical verification audits.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>User Resistance to Digital Workflow</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-warning">Medium</span> / <span class="badge badge-warning">Medium</span></td>
      <td>Senior Trust committee members used to paper ledgers finding digital tools difficult.</td>
      <td>Designed an ultra-clean, intuitive Admin table mimicking familiar ledger layouts; conducted two hands-on training sessions with printed SOP guides.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Legacy Codebase Clutter</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-info">Low</span> / <span class="badge badge-success">Certain</span></td>
      <td>Old static HTML files causing deployment ambiguity and maintenance overhead.</td>
      <td>Executed rigorous repository pruning in Sprint 8, deleting 11 legacy files and releasing a pristine v2.0 React architecture.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- SECTION 6 -->
<h2>6. Quality Assurance, Performance &amp; Security Audits</h2>
<p>
  The portal was evaluated against stringent quality benchmarks prior to production cutover:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Lighthouse Audit Score:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Performance: <strong>96 / 100</strong> (Desktop) | <strong>92 / 100</strong> (Mobile Slow 4G)</li>
      <li>Accessibility: <strong>100 / 100</strong> (Color contrast, semantic landmarks, ARIA tags)</li>
      <li>Best Practices: <strong>100 / 100</strong> (Clean console, modern web APIs)</li>
      <li>SEO: <strong>100 / 100</strong> (Structured meta tags, bilingual headings)</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Cross-Browser Compatibility:</strong> Verified on Google Chrome (v110+), Safari (iOS 15+), Mozilla Firefox, and Samsung Internet.</li>
  <li><strong>Form Validation Testing:</strong> 120 edge-case test combinations evaluated across valid/invalid phone numbers, duplicate references, boundary marks percentages, and null data states.</li>
  <li><strong>Zero Data Loss Guarantee:</strong> Local storage fail-safe for tracking state in case of sudden network disconnection during form review.</li>
</ul>

<!-- SECTION 7 -->
<h2>7. Operational Handover, Maintenance &amp; Post-Launch SLA</h2>
<p>
  The project transitioned into the operational maintenance phase under a 12-month Service Level Agreement (SLA):
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Support Window:</strong> Trust office hours (10:00 AM – 6:00 PM IST, Monday through Saturday).</li>
  <li><strong>Defect Resolution SLA:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Critical (Portal inaccessible / Application submission blocked): Resolution within <strong>4 hours</strong>.</li>
      <li>Major (Tracking discrepancy / Admin filtering issue): Resolution within <strong>12 hours</strong>.</li>
      <li>Minor (Cosmetic typo / text update): Resolution within <strong>48 hours</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Annual Maintenance Activities:</strong> Quarterly security reviews, node dependency patches, scholarship year rollover scripts (e.g. archiving 2026 data to initiate 2027 batch).</li>
</ol>

